response:
It is a right square pyramid. There are four edges at the base: each measures 10cm, so the sum of their lengths is 40cm. There are four edges rising from the base that are the same length; they are the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs 5 and 12 [the height and half the base, in some units]. By the Pythagorean Theorem, those edges measure {eq}\sqrt{5^2+12^2}=\sqrt{25+144}=\sqrt{169}=13.

{/eq} Thus the total length of the edges is \begin{align*}
40+13+13+13+13 &= \boxed{92}.
\end{align*}

